course: dictionary
lesson: 14720
title: Profanity: swearing and rude language
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Profanity means swearing, or rude and offensive language that can hurt or upset people. «The film had a 15 rating because of its profanity.» The clue is the rating: it tells you the film has language that is not suitable for young children.
explain: A profanity is one single swear word or rude expression. So profanity is the general idea, and a profanity is one example of it. «The chat moderator removed every profanity from the game.» Here the plural shows that there were several separate rude words.
explain: Schools, games and websites often ban profanity. «No profanity in our class, please.» Online chat filters block profanities, which means they stop rude words from appearing on screen. When you meet a new word, swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: In formal writing, profanity can also mean disrespect for holy things. «The sign warned visitors against profanity in the cathedral.» Here it is not about swearing at people. It is about showing no respect for something sacred, so read the clues around the word carefully.
fact: Profanity means swearing, or rude and offensive language.
fact: A profanity is one swear word or rude expression.
fact: «Use profanity» and «a string of profanities» are common phrases; «a string of» means a long row of them, one after another.
fact: A «profanity filter» is a tool that blocks rude words on websites and in online chat.
fact: In formal use, profanity means disrespect for holy things, not just rude talk.
exercise: «The game was rated for older players because of its profanity.» What does profanity mean here? | A kind of game played in parks | *Swearing and rude, offensive language | A prize for winning a race | Quiet, polite talk between friends
exercise: What is a profanity, meaning one example? | *One swear word or rude expression | A holy building with tall towers | A kind of computer game | A long, boring speech given at assembly
exercise: What does a profanity filter do? | It plays music during the chat | *It blocks rude words from showing up | It translates words into French | It makes the screen brighter
test: «The teacher said, "No profanity in our class, please."» What is the teacher asking the class not to do? | *Use swear words and rude language | Share their pencils | Sing loudly during lessons | Ask questions about the work
test: «The sign warned visitors against profanity in the cathedral.» In this sentence, profanity means: | *Showing disrespect for holy things | Being very cold inside the building | Losing a ticket at the door | Walking too slowly around the halls
exam: Which statement about profanity is correct? | Profanity is one swear word; a profanity is all of them together | Profanity is a kind of film; a profanity is a kind of game | Profanity and a profanity mean exactly the same, with no difference | *Profanity is the general idea of swearing; a profanity is one rude word or expression
